WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 3: Reflections.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:10.420
Unit 3 is called Reflections because it is all about looking
closely at the world around you and expressing what you

3
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:10.820
see,

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.760
think, and feel through poetry and reflective writing.

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.480
Poets use special tools to paint pictures with words,

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.220
and by the end of this unit you
will use those same tools yourself.

7
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.530
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:35.620
By the end of this unit, you will be able to identify and
explain similes, metaphors, and personification in poems.

9
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.500
you will also read and understand
different kinds of poetry, including haiku.

10
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.880
you will also count syllables and
understand how poets use rhythm and sound.

11
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.360
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:56.520
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: policy,
lobby, constitution, charter, legislative, mission.

13
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:02.160
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.400
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.950
The reading sequence includes Reflections:
source text 1 and Reflections: source text 2.

16
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.480
Read actively.

17
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.520
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.260
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.480
The first language focus is What
Are Comparatives and Superlatives?.

20
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.760
Why They Matter Comparatives and
superlatives are special forms of adjectives.

21
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.140
They help us compare people, places, things, and ideas.

22
00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:44.400
When we compare poems, stories, characters, or events,
we use these forms to say which is bigger, better,

23
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.520
more beautiful, or most exciting.

24
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:53.020
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.540
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Choral Verse Performance.

26
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:03.640
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.060
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.540
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.360
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:19.000
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.700
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:27.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
